{"question": "Bệnh nhân cao tuổi mắc bệnh Parkinson có tỷ lệ và mức độ nghiêm trọng của bệnh sâu răng khác biệt so với các bệnh lý răng miệng khác không?", "claim": "Tỷ lệ và mức độ nghiêm trọng của bệnh sâu răng ở người cao tuổi mắc bệnh Parkinson có thể khác biệt so với các bệnh lý răng miệng khác do các cơ chế bệnh sinh đặc hiệu.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "So sánh nhóm bệnh nhân cao tuổi mắc bệnh Parkinson với nhóm người cao tuổi khỏe mạnh cho thấy tỷ lệ và mức độ nghiêm trọng của bệnh sâu răng có sự khác biệt rõ rệt. Những thay đổi này xuất phát từ các cơ chế bệnh sinh đặc hiệu liên quan đến sự suy giảm vận động, khả năng vệ sinh răng miệng và lưu lượng nước bọt ở nhóm bệnh nhân thần kinh trung ương."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "In addition to pain relief, some of the included studies also yielded positive outcomes on lesion size reduction and mucosal healing. Again, since measurement methods as well as scores varied, these results could not be combined quantitatively. Recurrence rates post-PRP therapy also were not consistently reported among the studies, so we could conclude little about the long-term persistence of the effect achieved. 11 There was one study that reported a statistically significant superiority for the injectable PRF group over the steroid group. Conversely, a separate included study noted that patients treated with PRP exhibited higher rates of disease recurrence and adverse effects compared to those treated with intralesional triamcinolone acetonide (TA) after three months of follow-up. PRP also potentially acts to help mucosal regeneration rather than inflammation suppression, suggesting a"}, {"quote_id": "P1.Q2", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "new, yet potentially adjunct, mechanism of action. 12,13"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Table 5
Key recommendations - surgical treatment of apical periodontitis
Intervention | Grade and evidence-based recommendations | Expert consensus-based recommendations
Root resection versus non-surgical root canal retreatment or apical surgery | Weak (⇓) We do not suggest root resection techniques as an alternative to non-surgical root canal retreatment or apical surgery in the management of permanent teeth with apical periodontitis Quality of evidence: Tooth survival: Very low ⊕⊝⊝⊝ |"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "The two studies therefore suggest that AI can increase reader sensitivity, but they do not establish net clinical benefit. Their designs, case allocation, outcomes, and tradeoffs differed, and neither evaluated patient outcomes in routine care. Certainty for incremental clinician benefit was very low."}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "yet none have specifically addressed dental caries with a meta‐analytic approach. This omission represents a critical gap in the literature, as dental caries prevalence and severity may differ from other oral diseases in PD due to distinct etiopathogenic mechanisms [18, 19, 22]."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Efficiency of platelet-rich plasma in management of oral lichen planus: a systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "DISCUSSION"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Endodontic S3-level clinical practice guidelines: the European Society of Endodontology process and recommendations", "heading_path": ["Body", "Key clinical recommendations", "Evidenced-based recommendations relating to the surgical treatment of mature teeth with apical periodontitis"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Diagnostic Accuracy of Artificial Intelligence for Dental Caries Detection Across Clinical Imaging Modalities: A Systematic Review and Descriptive Synthesis", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Results", "3.5. Clinician Interpretation with AI Assistance"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Dental Caries Experience in Older Adults With Parkinson's Disease: A Systematic Review and Meta‐Analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Introduction"]}]}
