{"question": "Nghiên cứu về các dấu ấn sinh học C-Reactive Protein và Procalcitonin trong nhiễm trùng ổ răng sử dụng phương pháp thống kê nào để phân tích các biến liên tục?", "claim": "Các biến liên tục trong nghiên cứu về dấu ấn sinh học CRP và PCT đối với mức độ nặng của nhiễm trùng ổ răng được phân tích bằng các số đo độ phân tán như giá trị trung bình và trung vị.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Khi phân tích số liệu về các dấu ấn sinh học trong các nghiên cứu nhiễm trùng ổ răng, nhóm biến liên tục được đánh giá thông qua các tham số đặc trưng về độ phân tán dữ liệu như giá trị trung bình và trung vị để đảm bảo tính chính xác thống kê."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Morbidity and mortality rates are correlated with the severity of infections. In order to lower the incidence of morbidity and death, it is critical for the clinician to assess the severity of the odontogenic infection and implement an aggressive treatment protocol. C-reactive protein (CRP) and procalcitonin (PCT) are common biomarkers of sepsis."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Data were captured and coded using Excel. They were then cleaned and analysed using version 25.0 of Statistical Package for the Social Sciences. Continuous variables were analysed using measures of dispersion such as means and medians. Summaries were presented as tables, pie charts, or graphs. Categorical data, such as gender and levels of education, were summarised by proportions and percentages. Chi-squared and P value analyses were done to find any statistical difference between severity scores and demographics. A range for CRP and PCT was then determined for mild, moderate, and SOIs. The sensitivity and specificity of CRP and PCT were determined. Then, the diagnostic accuracy of PCT and CRP was determined using PPV and NPVs and area under the ROC curve."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "The findings of Magrini et al.[23] are consistent with those of this current study. When they analysed CRP and PCT together and in conjunction with a severity clinical assessment, CRP and PCT were valid biomarkers for diagnosis and prognosis. However, PCT attests to its increased value as a sepsis diagnostic marker. They, therefore, concluded that to accurately and quickly diagnose sepsis and infection, a multi-diagnostic instrument strategy is essential.[23] Ríos-Toro et al.[24] also concluded that combinations of biomarkers can enhance the identification of confirmed bacterial sepsis in most seriously ill patients. Still, in less difficult septic situations, CRP or PCT alone perform similarly well.[24] A systematic review and meta-analysis done by Tan et al.[25] reported that the entire area under the ROC curve for the diagnostic accuracy of procalcitonin (PCT) for sepsis was 0.85"}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q2", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "ng/mL. That of C-reactive protein (CRP) was 0.73 mg/L. Hence, PCT has a greater diagnosis specificity and accuracy than CRP.[25]"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Table 4
New severity classification for C-reactive protein (CRP) and procalcitonin (PCT)
Scoring criteria | Count of C-reactive protein results | Count of procalcitonin results
80.3 | 1 | 1"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Comparison of C-Reactive Protein and Procalcitonin as Biomarkers for Severity of Sepsis in Odontogenic Infection", "heading_path": ["Abstract", "Introduction:"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Comparison of C-Reactive Protein and Procalcitonin as Biomarkers for Severity of Sepsis in Odontogenic Infection", "heading_path": ["Body", "Materials and Methods"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Comparison of C-Reactive Protein and Procalcitonin as Biomarkers for Severity of Sepsis in Odontogenic Infection", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Comparison of C-Reactive Protein and Procalcitonin as Biomarkers for Severity of Sepsis in Odontogenic Infection", "heading_path": ["Body", "Results"]}]}
