{"question": "Phương pháp thống kê chính nào được sử dụng để phân tích các kết quả liên tục trong nghiên cứu tổng quan hệ thống về điều trị quá cảm ngà?", "claim": "Trong nghiên cứu tổng quan hệ thống và phân tích gộp về quá cảm ngà, các kết quả liên tục được phân tích bằng độ chênh trung bình chuẩn hóa (SMD) kết hợp với khoảng tin cậy 95% và mô hình hiệu ứng ngẫu nhiên.", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "- Trong nghiên cứu tổng quan hệ thống và phân tích gộp về quá cảm ngà, các kết quả liên tục được phân tích bằng độ chênh trung bình chuẩn hóa (SMD).\n- Phân tích cần kết hợp với khoảng tin cậy 95% để đánh giá độ chính xác.\n- Áp dụng mô hình hiệu ứng ngẫu nhiên nhằm đảm bảo tính khách quan và độ tin cậy của dữ liệu thống kê."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "(MD −66.70 MME). For analgesia, there was no statistically significant difference between LB and control in postoperative pain intensity (SMD −0.21; 95% CI −0.51 to 0.10) or cumulative pain scores (SMD −1.06; 95% CI −2.52 to 0.39) over 0-48 hours, with high heterogeneity in the latter (I² = 96.9%). Our findings indicate that while LB was associated with a significant reduction in opioid consumption, the effect size is not clinically meaningful, with a limited difference in postoperative pain. However, the limited number of included studies highlights the need for cautious interpretation, with further large-scale RCTs needed to validate these findings."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Meta-analysis was conducted using Review Manager (RevMan) version 5.4. Continuous outcomes were analysed using the standardised mean difference (SMD) with 95% confidence intervals. In anticipation of clinical and methodological heterogeneity across interventions, a random-effects model (DerSimonian–Laird method) was applied as the primary analytical approach. Statistical heterogeneity was quantified using the I2 statistic; values exceeding 50% were considered indicative of substantial heterogeneity. Subgroup analyses were pre-specified based on the category of advanced desensitizing modality. Publication bias was assessed visually using funnel plots. Formal statistical tests for funnel plot asymmetry (e.g., Egger's regression test) were not performed, as several subgroups contained fewer than ten studies, which renders such tests underpowered and their results unreliable per Cochrane"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "Handbook guidance."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "Biomimetic remineralising agents, specifically nano-hydroxyapatite (SMD = −0.87; 95% CI: −1.50 to −0.25) and bioactive glass (SMD = −1.08; 95% CI: −2.08 to −0.09), demonstrated the second-highest category of efficacy in this review. These agents act by releasing calcium and phosphate ions that precipitate as hydroxycarbonate apatite within and over dentinal tubule apertures, restoring mineral integrity at the dentin surface.45,46"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Laser therapies demonstrated the largest pooled effect sizes among the included interventions, producing the greatest magnitude of pain reduction across all subgroups (SMD = −2.11; 95% CI: −2.96 to −1.26; p < 0.001) however, these findings should be interpreted cautiously because of substantial heterogeneity and variations in laser parameters. All laser studies were pooled as a single subgroup; no further stratification by laser type was undertaken given the limited number of studies per device category. The substantial within-subgroup heterogeneity (I2 = 93%) reflects genuine variability in laser type, wavelength, power settings, treatment protocols, and follow-up durations across included trials, and prevents definitive conclusions about the relative superiority of any particular laser system.42,43"}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Efficacy of Liposomal Bupivacaine in Third Molar Extraction: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis", "heading_path": ["Abstract"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Efficacy of advanced treatment modalities of dentin hypersensitivity: A systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Methods", "Statistical analysis and data synthesis"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Efficacy of advanced treatment modalities of dentin hypersensitivity: A systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion", "Nano-hydroxyapatite and bioactive glass-based agents"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Efficacy of advanced treatment modalities of dentin hypersensitivity: A systematic review and meta-analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Discussion", "Laser-based modalities"]}]}
