{"question": "Thang đo Newcastle-Ottawa (NOS) đánh giá mấy nhóm tiêu chí chính và mức độ nguy cơ sai lệch dựa trên tổng số sao được phân loại như thế nào?", "claim": "Thang đo Newcastle-Ottawa (NOS) sử dụng hệ thống đánh giá tối đa chín sao qua ba nhóm tiêu chí, với tổng điểm từ 5 đến 7 sao được phân loại là nguy cơ sai lệch trung bình (fair risk).", "internal_evidence": [{"evidence_id": "I1", "content": "Quy trình đánh giá chất lượng các nghiên cứu quan sát thông qua thang đo Newcastle-Ottawa tập trung vào các khía cạnh lựa chọn đối tượng và khả năng so sánh giữa các nhóm nghiên cứu. Phương pháp này áp dụng hệ thống cho điểm chi tiết nhằm xác định mức độ tin cậy của tài liệu khoa học được tổng hợp trong các tổng quan hệ thống."}], "public_quote_options": [{"quote_id": "P1.Q1", "evidence_id": "P1", "text": "Participants were high risk in 22 estimates (78.6%); index test was high risk in 5 (17.9%); and target condition was high risk in 6 (21.4%). Overall applicability concern was high in 17 estimates (60.7%), low in 8 (28.6%), and based on insufficient information in 3 (10.7%). Detailed judgments are in Supplementary Files S2 and S4."}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q1", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "The quality of each included study was independently assessed by the two analysts to evaluate the possible risk of bias, and the Newcastle–Ottawa scale (NOS), as it provides a comprehensive framework for observational studies that focuses on three key domains: selection of study groups, comparability of groups, and outcome assessment to obtain a final score.35 The NOS is a star rating system that assigns a maximum of nine stars across three categories. Studies scoring three or four stars in selection, one or two stars in comparability, and two or three stars in outcome/exposure were considered of good quality. Studies with two stars in selection, one or two stars in comparability, and two or three stars in outcome/exposure were classified as fair quality. When the studies scored no stars or one star in selection, no stars in comparability, and no stars or one star in outcome/exposure,"}, {"quote_id": "P2.Q2", "evidence_id": "P2", "text": "they were considered of poor quality. In accordance with this method, a study is considered to have a low risk of bias (8 or 9 stars), a fair risk (5–7 stars), or a high risk of bias (< 5 stars). In this review, 24 studies with scores ≥ 5 were included for analysis."}, {"quote_id": "P3.Q1", "evidence_id": "P3", "text": "Table 4\nNewcastle-Ottawa Quality Assessment for retrospective studies. [16]\nComparability | (5) Comparability of cohorts (design/analysis) | ★"}, {"quote_id": "P4.Q1", "evidence_id": "P4", "text": "Two reviewers (SA, EH) assessed risk of bias using specific tools: the RoB 2.0 tool for randomized controlled trials [24] and the Newcastle–Ottawa Scale (NOS) for observational studies [25]. Any discrepancies between the reviewers were resolved by seeking the opinion of a third reviewer (AK)."}], "public_sources": [{"evidence_id": "P1", "title": "Diagnostic Accuracy of Artificial Intelligence for Dental Caries Detection Across Clinical Imaging Modalities: A Systematic Review and Descriptive Synthesis", "heading_path": ["Body", "3. Results", "3.2. Risk of Bias"]}, {"evidence_id": "P2", "title": "Prevalence and Risk of Dental Erosion Linked to Carbonated Drinks in Adolescents: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "MATERIALS AND METHODS", "Risk of Bias"]}, {"evidence_id": "P3", "title": "Efficacy of Liposomal Bupivacaine in Third Molar Extraction: A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis", "heading_path": ["Body", "Review"]}, {"evidence_id": "P4", "title": "Wisdom teeth removal and anterior alignment stability after orthodontic treatment—a systematic review", "heading_path": ["Body", "Materials and methods", "Quality assessment"]}]}
